{"term":"raid","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cb1c4fdff51eff3c03","definition":"A quick hostile or predatory incursion or invasion in a battle.","example":"Marauding chief! his sole delight / The moonlight raid, the morning fight.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["attack","foray","incursion"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:36cbaacd8d7f6ea25c","definition":"An attack or invasion for the purpose of making arrests, seizing property, or plundering.","example":"a police raid of a narcotics factory","pos":"noun","synonyms":["irruption"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bd69fce7b6d18b6dde","definition":"An attacking movement.","example":"The athletic Walker, one of Tottenham's more effective attacking elements with his raids from right-back, made a timely intervention after Rose had been dispossessed and even Aaron Lennon was needed to provide an interception in the danger zone to foil another attempt by the Russians.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ac00ea3a12a8d81e41","definition":"An activity initiated at or towards the end of a live broadcast by the broadcaster that sends its viewers to a different broadcast, primarily intended to boost the viewership of the receiving broadcaster. This is frequently accompanied by a message in the form of a hashtag that is posted in the broadcast's chat by the viewers.","example":"Now that Twitch is making raids an official part of the platform, however, some streamers think the new feature will make it easier to participate in the positive aspects of raiding.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet","register":"Internet","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fd4ef92dede669592a","definition":"A large group in a massively multiplayer online game, consisting of multiple parties who team up to defeat a powerful enemy.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet","register":"Internet","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:91dc7ce1007e165e9e","definition":"An event involving a group of users, often using bots and scripts, who join a server to harm it or harass its members.","example":"I used the tools discord gave me to prevent raids but he somehow knows a bypass, I use bots and they do help prevent it but just having him ping 90 guys once makes people bash me for an entire hour.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9a1d82a84b0da54977","definition":"To engage in a raid against.","example":"The police raided the gambling den.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid","caught raiding the cookie jar","raidable","raider","ramraid","unraided"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a72a34b82ce316716","definition":"To lure from another; to entice away from.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air raid","air-raid","Baedeker raid","bear raid","corporate raid","dawn raid","panty raid","raidproof","ram raid","ram-raid","Zoom raid","counterraid","caught raiding the cookie jar","raidable","raider","ramraid","unraided"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cbda5e5645370251e7","definition":"To indulge oneself by taking from.","example":"I raided the fridge for snacks.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[]